      "id": "pxfsotn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Parliament of India comprises the President, Lok Sabha (House of the People), and Rajya Sabha (Council of States).",
        "Lok Sabha is the directly elected lower house with a normal term of 5 years, subject to dissolution.",
        "Rajya Sabha is a permanent upper house where one-third of members retire every two years.",
        "Joint Sitting of Parliament under Article 108 resolves deadlocks between the two houses on ordinary bills."
      ],
      "id": "bl99585"
    },
