    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Money Bills (Article 110) can only be introduced in the Lok Sabha and require the prior recommendation of the President.",
        "The Speaker of the Lok Sabha presides over a Joint Sitting of Parliament, not the Vice President (Chairman of Rajya Sabha).",
        "Rajya Sabha enjoys exclusive powers under Article 249 to authorize Parliament to legislate on State List matters and Article 312 for All-India Services."
      ],
